# Process Checks

## 1 ps
Shows running processes.

```bash
ps

2. top
Shows live system processes.
Bash
top
Service Checks

3. systemctl status ssh
Checks SSH service status.
Bash
systemctl status ssh

4. systemctl list-units --type=service
Shows active services.
Bash
systemctl list-units --type=service
Log Checks

5. journalctl -u ssh
Shows logs of SSH service.
Bash
journalctl -u ssh

6. tail -n 20 /var/log/syslog
Shows last 20 log lines.
Bash
tail -n 20 /var/log/syslog

Mini Troubleshooting

Checked running processes using ps and top
Verified SSH service status
Viewed service logs using journalctl
Read system logs using tail
